==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Office Lady Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Call Center Cat''' when obtained from the [[Vacation Awakes!]] (may be dropped on the first stage but guaranteed on the second stage) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Vacation Queen is extremely weak on all fronts, relative to the units one must have to get her in the first place, which means she isn't really fit for use.

==='''True Form'''===
In early stages (relative to when she can first be obtained), Call Center Cat can be stacked so that Red enemies (e.g. [[Pigge]], [[Bore]] etc.) enter her range and get knocked back, thus pushing them behind other enemies or the base and allowing [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] units to be more effective. However, because of her long foreswing and lengthy attack frequency, it is probably best to help her with other anti-Red knockbackers. Later in the game, Call Center gets heavily outclassed by most gacha anti-Reds or even generalists like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]].

